    <solution><m>\mathbf{(a)}</m> Since <m>r=7</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{3\pi}{2}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=7\cos \frac{3\pi}{2}=7\cdot 0=0</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=7\sin \frac{3\pi}{2}=7\cdot -1=-7</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(0,-7)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(b)}</m> For <m>(5,\frac{\pi}{4})</m> we have <m>r=5</m> and <m>\theta=\frac{\pi}{4}</m>. Hence,
<me>x=r\cos\theta=5\cos \frac{\pi}{4}=5\cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}=3.53553</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=5\sin \frac{\pi}{4}=5\cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}=3.53553</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(3.53553,3.53553)</me>



<m>\mathbf{(c)}</m> Since <m>r=5</m> and <m>\theta =\frac{\pi}{3}</m>, we have:
<me>x=r\cos\theta=5\cos \frac{\pi}{3}=5\cdot \frac12=2.5</me>
<me>y=r\sin\theta=5\sin \frac{\pi}{3}=5\cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}=4.33013</me>
<me>\Downarrow</me>
<me>(x,y)=(2.5,4.33013)</me>


</solution>
